


   =====( SendNodeMsg V1.00 )=============================================


        Trion SendNodeMsg door.

        (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '94-'97. All rights reserved.

        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


   SendNodeMsg is a door that lets Users send short messages to users on
   other BBS nodes.


   It first shows a list of nodes that are available to send messages to.
   Then it will ask for a line of text to send to that node.
   If the choosen node is running and there is someone logged in,
   the message is displayed.
   Also above the message the name of the sender and the BBS node 
   number of the sender is shown.


   Use it by adding something like the folowing to the menu files
   where you want to use it.


Cmd "S" , 0-255
   CliDoor  "doors:SendNodeMsg/SendNodeMsg ~50"
EndCmd


   The "S" part is the command that starts the door and can be
   changed to fit your needs, the ~50 is the number of the BBS node
   it was started from and is needed to get information from the
   BBS node like the name of the user online.


